1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:05,094
Rebase is not magic. It rewrites your
commits, one by one.

2
00:00:06,644 --> 00:00:11,323
The command is git rebase main. One line,
no flags.

3
00:00:12,293 --> 00:00:14,249
That is the whole incantation.

4
00:00:15,799 --> 00:00:20,484
Merge keeps the history. Rebase rewrites
it into a clean line.

5
00:00:21,454 --> 00:00:23,685
Same code, new commits.

6
00:00:25,235 --> 00:00:30,919
Never rebase a shared branch. Pull before
you push. Push early and often.

7
00:00:31,889 --> 00:00:35,134
And squash your own mess before anyone
reads it.

8
00:00:36,684 --> 00:00:41,113
It is safe with one person. It is
dangerous with two people.

9
00:00:42,663 --> 00:00:47,843
Safe on your branch. Risky on main, where
everyone else is standing.

10
00:00:48,813 --> 00:00:50,193
Own branch only.

11
00:00:51,743 --> 00:00:56,566
Your branch, pull first, squash. That is
the whole habit.

12
00:00:58,116 --> 00:01:02,024
Rebase your own branch. Leave the shared
one alone.
